### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@email = admin@example.com
@password = replace-with-local-password
@csrfToken = replace-with-xsrf-cookie-value

### Log in; an HTTP client with a cookie jar retains both auth cookies
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Obtain the CSRF cookie and token for state-changing user API calls
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/csrf

# Copy the returned token (or the XSRF-TOKEN cookie value) into the
# X-XSRF-TOKEN header used by POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE examples.

### Rotate the refresh token and issue a new access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh

### Show the authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
